4. LICENSE KEY USAGE

MetaEdit can be installed and used free of charge. The Premium
edition adds the applying step of the studio workflows, further
delivery profiles and command-line automation, as the edition table
shows, and requires the purchase of a Premium license key.

A Premium license key is personal to one person:

  - A key may be used on up to 3 computers at the same time. You can
    release a computer in Arctisoft Studio Hub to use the license on
    another one. A computer that has not used the license for 45 days is
    released automatically.
  - Sharing, publishing or distributing your license key is prohibited.
  - A license may be passed on only as a whole, using the transfer
    function in Arctisoft Studio Hub. After a transfer you may no longer
    use it.
  - Keys that are misused or obtained by fraud may be deactivated.

The computers using a license are recorded solely to apply these limits,
not to track individual user activity. The License Agreement in Arctisoft
Studio Hub states the complete terms.


5. DATA PROCESSING AND PRIVACY

Controller:
  Arctisoft Studio / Bernd Julian Hagen
  Contact: support@arctisoft-studio.com

Cloud Settings Sync (optional and disabled by default):
  When you enable sync in Settings while signed in to an Arctisoft account,
  the following preferences are processed:

  - ID3 version and text encoding preferences
  - tag-container preservation preferences
  - artwork conversion, quality, size, and picture-type preferences
  - enabled Auto-Tag sources

  Storage: Supabase (EU region). Data is encrypted in transit (TLS 1.2+).
  Legal basis: Legitimate interest (Art. 6 para. 1 lit. f GDPR).
  You can disable synchronization at any time in MetaEdit. Signing in also
  sends a device identifier, device name, and the application name to the
  Arctisoft licensing service so active licensed devices can be managed.

Auto-Tag Feature (opt-in per lookup):
  When you trigger an automatic metadata lookup, the following external
  services are contacted:

  - AcoustID (acoustid.org) - audio fingerprint identification
  - MusicBrainz (musicbrainz.org) - music metadata database
  - Discogs (discogs.com) - release metadata when you provide a Discogs token
  - iTunes Search API (apple.com) - cover art and metadata

  A short audio fingerprint of the selected file is transmitted solely
  for identification. No audio data is stored beyond the request.

Cover Art Search (opt-in per search):
  Your search query (artist name, album name) is sent to MusicBrainz
  and Cover Art Archive for album artwork lookup. No other data is
  transmitted.

Lyrics Lookup (opt-in per search):
  Track title, artist, and album search terms are sent to LRCLIB (lrclib.net)
  to retrieve synchronized or plain-text lyrics.

Software Updates:
  MetaEdit can check its public GitHub release feed for updates. These
  requests include normal network information and the current application
  version, but never include media files or file metadata.

No personal files, audio content, or file metadata are transmitted to
Arctisoft Studio without your explicit action.

Data Retention:
  Cloud settings and account data can be deleted through Arctisoft account
  management or by contacting Arctisoft Studio support.
  No analytics or tracking data is collected.


